BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Family violence intervention order changes (by this date)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261111
DTSTAMP:20261019T000000Z
UID:fv-stalking-2026-nov@plainenglishlaw.vic-commencements
CATEGORIES:Victoria,No later than
DESCRIPTION:Courts must consider whether someone has been misidentified as
  the main aggressor\, intervention orders can no longer be made against ch
 ildren under 12\, and final orders against adults default to 24 months unl
 ess the court sets another period.\n\nDate type: No later than (could star
 t earlier by proclamation)\nJurisdiction: Victoria\nWho it affects: People
  involved in family violence intervention order cases\; courts\; police\n
 \nOfficial source: https://judicialcollege.vic.edu.au/resources/justice-le
 gislation-amendment-family-violence-stalking-and-other-matters-act-2026-gu
 ide\nCommencement source: https://www.legislation.vic.gov.au/sites/default
 /files/2026-08/Commencement-information-for-Acts-enacted-this-year.pdf\nNo
 te: Judicial College of Victoria guide gives 10 Nov 2026. Support: 1800RES
 PECT 1800 737 732\; emergencies 000.\n\nLast checked: 2026-10-19\nGeneral 
 information only\, not legal advice.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://judicialcollege.vic.edu.au/resources/justice-legislation-amend
 ment-family-violence-stalking-and-other-matters-act-2026-guide
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
