BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Privacy policies must explain automated decisions
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261210
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261211
DTSTAMP:20261019T000000Z
UID:cth-privacy-automated-decisions@plainenglishlaw.vic-commencements
CATEGORIES:Commonwealth,Fixed date
DESCRIPTION:Organisations covered by the Privacy Act must say in their pri
 vacy policy when computer programs use personal information to make\, or s
 ubstantially help make\, decisions that could significantly affect people.
 \n\nDate type: Fixed date\nJurisdiction: Commonwealth\nWho it affects: Bus
 inesses and agencies covered by the Privacy Act\; consumers\n\nOfficial so
 urce: https://www.legislation.gov.au/C2024A00128/asmade/text\nCommencement
  source: https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/australian-privacy-principles/aus
 tralian-privacy-principles-guidelines/chapter-1-app-1-open-and-transparent
 -management-of-personal-information\n\nLast checked: 2026-10-19\nGeneral i
 nformation only\, not legal advice.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.legislation.gov.au/C2024A00128/asmade/text
END:VEVENT
