BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AML/CTF independent evaluation deadline (existing businesses) (dea
 dline)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270331
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270401
DTSTAMP:20261019T000000Z
UID:cth-austrac-independent-evaluation@plainenglishlaw.vic-commencements
CATEGORIES:Commonwealth,Compliance deadline
DESCRIPTION:Businesses already regulated by AUSTRAC that have had an indep
 endent review must complete their first independent evaluation under the r
 eformed rules by 31 March 2027\, or 4 years after their last review if tha
 t is later.\n\nDate type: Compliance deadline\nJurisdiction: Commonwealth
 \nWho it affects: Existing AUSTRAC reporting entities (e.g. banks\, remitt
 ers\, gambling businesses)\n\nOfficial source: https://www.austrac.gov.au/
 about-us/legislation/updates-legislation/amlctf-transitional-rules-2026\nN
 ote: A compliance deadline\, not a new law starting.\n\nLast checked: 2026
 -10-19\nGeneral information only\, not legal advice.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.austrac.gov.au/about-us/legislation/updates-legislation/am
 lctf-transitional-rules-2026
END:VEVENT
