BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Renting: lease-break cap\, spare keys and more (by this date)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270601
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270602
DTSTAMP:20261019T000000Z
UID:renting-jun-2027@plainenglishlaw.vic-commencements
CATEGORIES:Victoria,No later than
DESCRIPTION:A cap on what renters can be ordered to pay for ending a fixed
 -term lease early\, rental providers can't unreasonably refuse a request f
 or a spare key or fob\, an offence to refuse a renter who pays bond direct
 ly to the RTBA\, and a ban on refusing to rent to someone because of famil
 y or personal violence.\n\nDate type: No later than (could start earlier b
 y proclamation)\nJurisdiction: Victoria\nWho it affects: Renters\, rental 
 providers and agents\n\nOfficial source: https://www.consumer.vic.gov.au/h
 ousing/renting/new-changes-to-the-rental-laws\nCommencement source: https:
 //www.gazette.vic.gov.au/gazette/Gazettes2026/GG2026S497.pdf\nNote: CAV li
 sts these as 1 June 2027. The cap applies to fixed terms of 5 years or les
 s.\n\nLast checked: 2026-10-19\nGeneral information only\, not legal advic
 e.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.consumer.vic.gov.au/housing/renting/new-changes-to-the-ren
 tal-laws
END:VEVENT
